  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The bolt's path and forks, the static arcs, the sparks and the scorch vary per cast. The 0.38 s charge and the strike at 380 ms stay fixed so the hit always lands on the same frame."
  },
  "director_notes": "A thrown lightning bolt at one target, built to sit next to the existing lightning without repeating it: Chain Arc hops between several enemies with thin snappy arcs, Ball Lightning flies an orb, Charge-Discharge is a sustained beam, Sky Strike and Boss Storm Call come from above. Choices: (1) the charge is on the caster's whole body (crackles around the body and the feet, a throbbing aura) instead of in a hand orb, 0.38 s, so the wind-up reads at a glance; (2) one thick bolt from hand to the target's chest (7-9 px, one level of forks) with two re-strikes 80 ms apart, the classic thrown-thunderbolt shape; (3) a warm yellow palette with pale blue sparks, so it reads apart from the white-blue and violet bolts in the library. Medium weight, side view hero. Sound: buzz while charging, crack on the lash, rapid zaps on the re-strikes, a quiet crackle tail."
}
